WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
Speaker 1: All right. On Monday, I told&nbsp;
you some states are looking very strongly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:16.240
at going in the direction of considering dropping&nbsp;
mask mandates, either indoor at businesses and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.920
or in schools. Over the last 48 hours&nbsp;
since I came to you with that report,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.280
it is accelerating dramatically. More and more&nbsp;
localities, more and more states talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.400
no more masks as of some date in the relatively&nbsp;
near future could be February could be March.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.680
And the question now is, is this the right time?&nbsp;
Not everybody agrees that it is. I don't actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.520
have an answer. And so anybody trying to read into&nbsp;
whether I think it's time to end masking or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.440
I'm not completely sure. I think there's&nbsp;
definitely a discussion to be had. Let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:55.040
go through some of the news. ABC reporting&nbsp;
indoor masking coming to an end in New York.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:02.000
Is it hopeful or hopeful? I never remember Hochul&nbsp;
expected to make an announcement Wednesday. It is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.080
anticipated that the governor of New York will&nbsp;
announce the end of the indoor mask mandate in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:11.600
New York state on Wednesday, but the city mandate&nbsp;
will remain in place. The state mandate requires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.240
masks to be worn inside businesses where&nbsp;
vaccination status was not being checked.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.360
It is set to expire Thursday, and the New York&nbsp;
Times reports that the governor will rescind it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.280
Connecticut and New Jersey are already&nbsp;
among a handful of states with plans to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:33.680
ease ease mask mandates in schools. The governor&nbsp;
of New York has not made the same move. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.000
she held a call with school superintendents&nbsp;
who believe an announcement is coming soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:44.720
The governor is expected to extend the mask&nbsp;
mandate, passed its February 21st expiration&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:52.000
and through winter break. Meanwhile, Illinois&nbsp;
is expected to announce an end or rollback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.680
of certain mask rules. CNN reporting the governors&nbsp;
of New York and Illinois are expected to announce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:04.240
the end of or a plan to roll back certain COVID&nbsp;
mitigation requirements involving masks today.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.320
I already told you about New York. In Illinois,&nbsp;
Governor J.B. Pritzker will likely announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.480
Wednesday a path for ending the state's&nbsp;
indoor mask mandate in most public places.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:23.280
There is also increasingly pressure in&nbsp;
Massachusetts on the Gov. Charlie Baker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:30.640
to make some kind of off ramp type statement. Many&nbsp;
cities and towns already going in that direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:37.760
in California, California's indoor mask mandate&nbsp;
will end next week for vaccinated people, citing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:43.840
a 65 percent drop in COVID cases since the peak&nbsp;
of Amick Run. California will end its statewide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.840
indoor mask mandate for vaccinated individuals&nbsp;
next week. Gov. Gavin Newsom announced Monday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:56.800
on Feb. 15, California's statewide indoor mask&nbsp;
requirement will expire. Unvaccinated people must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:02.160
still wear masks indoors. Less than 20 percent&nbsp;
of the state's population remain unvaccinated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.760
according to data. The Biden administration&nbsp;
has not yet offered a plan or roadmap for how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:13.040
to handle this, so a couple of different things&nbsp;
here. Number one, not everybody agrees about this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.240
One example is the former Surgeon General&nbsp;
Jerome Adams. Now, Jerome Adams was not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:23.760
exactly the voice of reason when Donald Trump&nbsp;
was president. So there are people who would say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:30.320
I don't care what Jerome Adams says, but Jerome&nbsp;
Adams tweeting quote, I respectfully disagree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.840
with many of my colleagues who are espousing the&nbsp;
idea that prematurely dropping mask mandates will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:41.440
somehow make it easier to bring them back if and&nbsp;
when things get worse again. How'd that work out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:48.800
when CDC said vaccinated could unmask last summer?&nbsp;
He went on to say, how do I define premature?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:54.480
Well, by looking at spread impact and protection&nbsp;
spread seven day average still highest since April&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:02.560
of last year, impact over 2500 deaths yesterday.&nbsp;
Protection only 22 percent of those five to 11&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.600
and 56 percent of 12 to 17 year olds&nbsp;
are vaccinated. Exit the highway early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:15.760
trip takes longer. I'm not sure if this is the&nbsp;
right thing to do or not. On the one hand, Jerome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:22.560
Adams is right, which is the numbers are still&nbsp;
not looking great. That being said, we know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:28.640
the numbers significantly lag what is going on.&nbsp;
There are states with cases down 85 to 90 percent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:36.000
Vaccines are so widely available, the death&nbsp;
rate is so incredibly low for the vaccinated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:42.960
that there becomes a question of what is the&nbsp;
milestone. And if there is not a reversal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:48.960
if we say, well, cases are down in the country,&nbsp;
about 70 percent in some states they're down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:54.240
85 to 90 percent. If we give it one more month&nbsp;
and that continues and there isn't a reversal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:00.560
There really won't be anything else to wait&nbsp;
for in the sense that it's not going away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.880
anytime soon. There's going to be a low level&nbsp;
again if in the next month there's not a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:12.320
variant that causes cases to spike in a month,&nbsp;
cases will be really at what we might call an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.560
endemic level doesn't mean the cases are mild.&nbsp;
It might or it might not, but we're talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.040
about the case levels. There's a question of what&nbsp;
would we be waiting for at that point in time?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:28.000
And there's not really a clear answer. And so&nbsp;
that's where the if not in two to four weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:35.760
then when becomes a relevant question. People who&nbsp;
choose to remain unvaccinated do so at their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:43.440
risk. And as always, the question then becomes&nbsp;
What about the immunocompromised? And that is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:50.800
situation where those folks say, Well, I've gotten&nbsp;
vaccinated, but I still really can't do anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.080
because I might still catch it and I'm at higher&nbsp;
risk. And that's a serious question. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:02.080
a lot of those people haven't been doing anything&nbsp;
anyway. So it is a sort of chicken egg thing where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.480
if the immunocompromised folks that&nbsp;
have been staying home all this time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:14.640
are already staying home, then what is the reason&nbsp;
to delay ending the mask mandates for those who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.160
are not staying home? It's complicated. I'm&nbsp;
going to admit that it's very complicated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.160
but the question I keep coming&nbsp;
back to is, if not in a month,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:26.320
then what is the milestone that we are waiting&nbsp;
for? And I've not heard a good answer to that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:33.200
which suggests continuing on with some of&nbsp;
this stuff. The schools question is a separate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:38.960
question, particularly when in schools you've got&nbsp;
a population that has a lower vaccination rate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:45.200
I'm thinking out loud along with you guys, and&nbsp;
I know that in my audience there are people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:50.720
are saying, This is it. It's time for the personal&nbsp;
responsibility phase and everything and let people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.680
decide for themselves what level of risk to accept&nbsp;
like we do during flu season. Some people already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.080
would wear a mask during flu season or stay home.&nbsp;
That one side of my audience, the other side of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.520
my audience says, Do nothing. We need to keep&nbsp;
masking for at least the entire year. We should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:11.760
